/* ~/.config/rofi/config.rasi
 *
 * ╔════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
 * ║  THIS FILE IS YOURS.                                                   ║
 * ║  LYNX created it once and will never touch it again.                   ║
 * ╚════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
 *
 * This import is the only link between you and LYNX. rofi expands ~ in import
 * paths; if you moved the repo, fix the path.
 */

@import "~/dotfiles/lynx/config/rofi/lynx.rasi"

/* ─── Your overrides ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * Everything below the import wins, because rasi keeps the last value it
 * parses. Options go in `configuration { }`, looks go in widget sections.
 * Use palette names instead of hex (@primary, @surface, @on-surface, ...) so
 * your changes follow the wallpaper once theming lands. For example:
 *
 *   configuration            { icon-theme: "Adwaita"; }
 *   window                   { width: 800px; }
 *   listview                 { lines: 12; }
 *   element selected.normal  { background-color: @tertiary; }
 *
 * No restart needed: rofi reads its config fresh every time it opens.
 * If something looks wrong, rofi's warnings are in ~/.cache/lynx/rofi.log
 */
